Java object serialization can be super dangerous as it just works on any class that implements serializable.<p>That means if the shape of your object is something like<p><pre><code>    class Foo implements Serializable {
      SerializableFunction bar;

      void doBar() {
        bar.apply();
      }
    }
</code></pre>
You&#x27;ve created a class which an attacker can plug in any object which implements `SerializableFunction` into `bar`.  That includes externally created functions!<p>Here&#x27;s an article detailing exactly how that works: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.baeldung.com&#x2F;java-serialize-lambda" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.baeldung.com&#x2F;java-serialize-lambda</a>
